course: dictionary
lesson: 12068
title: Cleanliness and keeping clean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cleanliness is a noun. It names the state of being clean, and the habit of keeping things clean. You can say «good cleanliness», but you cannot count it, so there is no plural form.
explain: Look at the word parts: clean, plus -liness. The ending turns a describing word into a naming word, just as lazy becomes laziness. When you see -liness, think of a thing or a quality, not an action.
explain: «Cleanliness stops germs spreading, so wash your hands before lunch.» The words germs and hands tell you the sentence is about hygiene, keeping yourself free from germs. Cleanliness means the care that keeps germs away.
explain: «Personal cleanliness» means keeping yourself clean, such as washing, brushing your teeth and changing your clothes. The word can also be about places, like a clean kitchen or a hospital ward.
fact: Cleanliness means being clean, or keeping things clean.
fact: Personal cleanliness means keeping your own body and clothes clean.
fact: Cleanliness is important in health and science lessons because it helps stop germs spreading.
fact: «Cleanliness is next to godliness» is an old saying that links keeping clean with being good.
fact: Cleanliness is uncountable, so say «good cleanliness», not «two cleanlinesses».
exercise: «Wash your hands before you eat, because cleanliness stops germs spreading.» What does cleanliness mean here? | Running very fast | *Keeping things clean, so germs cannot spread | Being very tired | Having a loud voice
exercise: «Our class is learning about cleanliness and hygiene.» Which word names the state of being clean? | class | about | *cleanliness | learning
exercise: Which of these is an example of personal cleanliness? | Reading a long book | Running in the park | Painting the garden fence | *Brushing your teeth and washing your face
test: «The kitchen shone with cleanliness after the chef scrubbed every surface.» What does cleanliness mean here? | *Being very clean, with every surface scrubbed | Being very late | Being very loud | Being very dirty
test: Ben says, «Cleanliness is next to godliness.» What is the old saying suggesting? | Clean things are always boring | Dirty hands are the best | Only grown-ups need to wash | *Keeping clean is linked with being good
exam: Which word means the habit of keeping yourself and your home clean? | *cleanliness | cleaner | cleaned | clean
